        "h": "Peter Medak, director of <em>The Changeling</em>, dies at 88",
        "p": "Peter Medak died on Tuesday, October 27, in Los Angeles, Dread Central reports, citing Variety. He was 88. His 1980 film <em>The Changeling</em> starred George C. Scott; his horror work also included <em>Species II</em> and episodes of <em>Tales from the Crypt</em>, <em>Masters of Horror</em> and <em>Hannibal</em>.",
        "src": "Dread Central",
        "url": "https://www.dreadcentral.com/news/595622/peter-medak-director-of-the-changeling-has-passed-away-at-88/",
        "date": "2026-11-01"
      },
      {
        "h": "Vinegar Syndrome opens in Minneapolis",
        "p": "Vinegar Syndrome has opened a store in Minneapolis, its latest after Bridgeport, Denver, Toronto and Pittsburgh. Blu-ray.com paid a visit.",
        "src": "Blu-ray.com",
        "url": "https://www.blu-ray.com/news/?id=39201",
        "date": "2026-10-31"
      },
      {
        "h": "The <em>Terrifier</em> trilogy returns to theaters",
        "p": "All three <em>Terrifier</em> films (2016, 2022 and 2024) are back in theaters on consecutive nights around Halloween, presented by Dead by Daylight ahead of Art the Clown's arrival in the game, Rue Morgue reports.",
        "src": "Rue Morgue",
        "url": "https://rue-morgue.com/terrifier-trilogy-returns-to-theatres-for-halloween",
        "date": "2026-10-30"
      },
      {
        "h": "The make-up behind Hammer's monsters",
        "p": "The National Science and Media Museum in Bradford holds the Ashton &amp; Leakey Collection: sketches, prosthetics, glass eyes and fangs from Hammer make-up artists Roy Ashton and Phil Leakey, covering <em>The Curse of Frankenstein</em> (1957), <em>Dracula</em> (1958), <em>The Mummy</em> (1959) and <em>The Gorgon</em> (1964). Great British Life reports the museum is opening the collection up.",
        "src": "Science Museum Group",
        "url": "https://collection.sciencemuseumgroup.org.uk/objects/co8066758/ashton-leakey-collection",
        "date": "2026-10-29"
      },
      {
        "h": "<em>Smile</em> and <em>A Quiet Place</em> join the Hellbreak card game",
        "p": "Monsters from <em>Smile</em>, <em>Sleepy Hollow</em> and <em>A Quiet Place</em> are joining Spin Master's Hellbreak trading card game, Rue Morgue reports. The game was built with Universal; its first reveals were Count Dracula, the Bride of Frankenstein and the shark from <em>Jaws</em>.",
        "src": "Rue Morgue",
        "url": "https://rue-morgue.com/paramounts-horror-icons-join-hellbreak-trading-card-game",
        "date": "2026-10-28"
      },
      {
        "h": "Kurosawa and Shimizu direct Disney+'s <em>Night Tales Club</em>",
        "p": "<em>Night Tales Club</em>, a six-part Disney+ anthology adapted from stories by Ichi Sawamura, premieres in January 2027. Kiyoshi Kurosawa, Takashi Shimizu and Shinzo Katayama are among the six episode directors; Takayuki Yamada stars in the framing story as a wealthy man who pays for accounts of the unexplained.",
        "src": "Dread Central",
        "url": "https://www.dreadcentral.com/streaming-home-video/594755/disney-unleashes-japanese-horror-all-stars-for-new-supernatural-anthology-series-night-tales-club/",
        "date": "2026-10-27"
      },
      {
        "h": "Hammer's uncut <em>Dracula</em> collector's edition",
        "p": "Hammer's Limited Collector's Edition of <em>Dracula</em> (1958) was scheduled for October 26, Dread Central reported: seven discs (two 4K UHD, five Blu-ray) carrying five versions of the film, including the uncensored UK cut rebuilt from Japanese reels found in Warner Bros.' archive, plus a 200-page book and a 60-page <em>House of Hammer</em> comic reprint.",
        "src": "Dread Central",
        "url": "https://www.dreadcentral.com/streaming-home-video/587183/hammers-uncut-dracula-gets-a-blood-red-4k-collectors-edition-with-footage-missing-for-68-years/",
        "date": "2026-10-26"
      }
